<div class="container">
<div class="card-body">

  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-6 offset-md-3">
      <h2>Privacy, security and data sovereignty</h2>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-6 offset-md-3">
      <h5>Your data never leaves your device</h5>
      <p><img src="/assets/images/shield.png" style="width: 3em; float:left; margin-right:0.5em;" /> Causal
        Wizard runs entirely in your browser. When you upload a CSV or Excel file, it's read and processed
        locally on your own computer &mdash; it is never sent to us, or to any server. We have no backend, no
        database, and no way to see your data even if we wanted to.
      </p>

      <h5>Where your data is stored</h5>
      <p>Your dataset, causal diagram and study configuration are kept in your browser's local storage
        (IndexedDB), on your own device only. Nothing is uploaded, and nothing is synced to us or to the cloud.
        If you switch browsers or devices, you'll need to re-upload your data there too.
      </p>

      <h5>Deleting data</h5>
      <p>Since nothing is stored on our servers, there's nothing for us to delete. To remove your data, clear
        this site's data from your browser (via your browser's site settings), or simply stop using the
        dataset/study in the app. Deletion is immediate and entirely under your control.
      </p>

      <div class="card mb-2">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h5 id="privacy">Privacy and data protection</h5>
          <p>
            We don't collect any personal information about you. There's no sign-up, no account, and no email
            address required to use Causal Wizard.
          </p>
          <p>
            We do not currently use any tracking, analytics or advertising on this site. If that ever changes,
            this page will be updated to say so &mdash; and it will never involve sending your uploaded data
            anywhere.
          </p>
          <p>
            Once you've finished your analysis in the wizard, you'll download a study configuration file (JSON)
            to run against your data using the notebooks we provide. That step also runs on your own computer,
            or in a notebook environment you choose (such as Google Colab) &mdash; we're not involved in it at
            all.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>


    </div>
  </div>

</div>

</div>
